### Phone-side throw computation

**`controller/js/throw.js:163-199`**:

```js
export function computeThrowDescriptor(samples, tuning = ThrowTuning) {
  if (!samples || samples.length === 0) return null;
  const release = samples[samples.length - 1];              // newest sample
  const windowStart = release.t - tuning.swingWindowMs;     // 1500 ms
  let peak = null;
  for (const sample of samples) {
    if (sample.t < windowStart) continue;
    if (peak === null || sample.power > peak.power) peak = sample;
  }
  if (peak === null || peak.power < tuning.minValidPeakAccel) return null;   // 3 m/s²
  const releaseDelayMs = Math.abs(release.t - peak.t);
  return {
    power: normalize01(peak.power, tuning.minPeakAccel, tuning.maxPeakAccel),   // 6 → 35
    timingQuality: 1 - normalize01(releaseDelayMs, 0, tuning.peakWindowMs),     // 250 ms
    aimDeg: clamp(toGameYaw(release.dYaw), -tuning.maxAimDeg, tuning.maxAimDeg),// ±180
    attackAngleDeg: clamp(release.dBeta, tuning.minAttackDeg, tuning.maxAttackDeg), // ±60
    rollDeg: release.dGamma,
    spinRate: Math.hypot(release.rotationRate.alpha, release.rotationRate.beta, release.rotationRate.gamma),
    peakAccel: peak.power, releaseDelayMs, sampleCount: samples.length,
  };
}
```

The `release` sample is the newest ring-buffer entry (≤16 ms old at 60 Hz). Aim is taken live to the last frame — as documented. The release is bound to `touchend` in HOLD mode (`app.js:134-135`) / `touchstart` in TAP mode (`app.js:126-127`).

